# Local Green Then Push

When changing app behaviour, bug fixes, UI states, data packs, or admin logic:

- Update `PLAN.md` first when the work changes the roadmap or planned scope.
- Use test-first development where practical: add or update the focused test, confirm it fails for the expected missing behaviour, then implement the change.
- Run the focused test and the full local suite (`node --test`) after implementation.
- Only push to `main` after the local focused and full checks are green.
- After pushing, verify the live GitHub Pages URL or live Supabase Edge Function when the change affects deployed behaviour.
- Tell the user what passed locally and whether the live deployment is ready for their online testing.

If a change is documentation-only or cannot reasonably have a failing automated test, say so explicitly and still run the relevant local checks before pushing.
